## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to convert dependency graphs into scheduling via topological order; checks understanding of longest-path DP on DAG, cycle detection, and clear complexity analysis.

## Key Concepts
- Topological sort (Kahn / DFS)
- DAG longest path DP
- Cycle detection
- Complexity analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
function earliestFinishTimes(n, edges, durations) {
  const adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);
  for (const [u, v] of edges) { adj[u].push(v); indeg[v]++; }
  const q = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  const finish = durations.slice();
  let seen = 0;
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    seen++;
    for (const v of adj[u]) {
      finish[v] = Math.max(finish[v], finish[u] + durations[v]);
      if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
    }
  }
  if (seen !== n) throw new Error('Cycle detected');
  return finish;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for multiple start times or optional prerequisites?
- How does the solution change if edge weights represent communication delay instead of task duration?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced DP: partitioning with a quadratic segment cost, requiring prefix sums and both memoized and tabulated solutions. Demonstrates recurrence derivation, base cases, and complexity reasoning.

## Key Concepts

- DP on partitions
- Prefix sums for O(1) range sums
- Time: O(N^2 K); Space: O(NK) (or O(N))
- Edge-case handling for N < K

## Code Example

```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, K){
  const N = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(N+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<N;i++) pref[i+1]=pref[i]+A[i];
  const INF = 1e18;
  const dp = Array.from({length:N+1}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(INF));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=N;i++) dp[i][1]=(pref[i]-pref[0])**2;
  for(let k=2;k<=K;k++){
    for(let i=1;i<=N;i++){
      for(let j=k-1;j<=i-1;j++){
        dp[i][k] = Math.min(dp[i][k], dp[j][k-1] + (pref[i]-pref[j])**2);
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[N][K];
}
```

